# Keep Docker build contexts small, reproducible, and free of host-only data.
# Required build inputs intentionally remain available: stack.yaml,
# stack.yaml.lock, package.yaml/*.cabal files, Haskell src/app/test trees,
# hmem-server/frontend package manifests + Elm/Vite source, and migrations.
# Future Dockerfiles should COPY dependency manifests first (Stack package
# manifests, frontend package.json/package-lock.json/elm.json) and source,
# static source assets, tests, and migrations after dependency layers. Use
# npm ci so package-lock.json is the deterministic frontend input.

# VCS and local workspace metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.hmem.workspace

# Stack and Cabal build outputs
.stack-work*/
**/.stack-work*/
dist/
dist-newstyle/
**/dist/
**/dist-newstyle/
cabal-dev/
**/cabal-dev/
.cabal-sandbox/
**/.cabal-sandbox/
cabal.sandbox.config
**/cabal.sandbox.config
cabal.project.local
cabal.project.local~
**/cabal.project.local
**/cabal.project.local~
*.cabal.bak
**/*.cabal.bak

# Haskell compiler/test artifacts
*.o
*.hi
*.dyn_o
*.dyn_hi
*.chi
*.chs.h
*.hp
*.prof
*.aux
*.eventlog
*.tix
.hpc/
**/.hpc/
